WEBVTT

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.630
E-Excuse me!

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.320
I was about to get on with my weigh-in...

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.520
Wh... Why are you waving that
 disgusting thing in our faces?

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.050
I had to put off a lot of weight.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.540
So I was taking off my briefs just to be on the safe side.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.030
This is a title match. You need to act like it.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.180
You have both passed the weigh-in.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.430
You really cut it close.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.680
The guy said I passed, didn't he?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.060
Can we have you gentlemen shake hands for tomorrow's match?

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.160
Sure.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.310
Let's make this a good one, okay?

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:51.820
A Kodak moment! {Kodak no longer does photography, ain't it sad... -FAb}

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:58.950
H-Hey!

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.660
I'll pass.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.690
Why?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.200
I would have acquiesced if we were like-minded people.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.640
However...

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.540
That man is not worthy

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:11.960
to receive my handshake!

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.170
He's not a boxer as far as I'm concerned.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.130
The Frog Punch?

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:20.760
I'll squash it the moment he tries that asinine move.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.770
You need to hit the tapes again.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.360
You really think I'd show up to a title match

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.480
without a little something up my sleeve?

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.030
Is it a new move?!

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.450
You developed something deadlier than the Frog Punch?!

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:45.290
It's just another weird little trick that won't work against me.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.330
"Weird little trick"?

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.590
I know I've won and lost my share of matches.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.590
But I've learned from my experiences.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.070
And you'll see how much I've
 learned come our title match.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.970
You'll soon realize that I <i>always</i>  do my homework.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.570
I didn't become the champion by chance.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.950
I've also fought my matches in a simple, straightforward fashion.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.520
You may fool around with your "homework," but I'm

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.110
an actual workhorse.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.560
This is gonna be great!

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.720
"I'll squash your
 Frog," he says?

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.900
That smug prick!

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.400
<i>I lost again.</i>

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.530
<i>Wish </i>I <i>was a boxer who had nice footwork.</i>

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.500
<i>He swooped around like a bird avoiding my punches.</i>

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.750
<i>This little guy's just like me.</i>

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.240
<i>He can't fly even if he wants to.</i>

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.010
<i>Guess that means you'll have to bounce up.</i>

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.390
<i>This is it!</i>

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.360
The idea may have been juvenile,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.630
but I mastered my Frog Punch with confidence!

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.600
I ain't gonna lose!

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.990
I won't let him squash my Frog!

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.370
Itagaki!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.370
Kimura-san! Senpai!

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:29.850
Gosh, nothing's better than fluids and sweets after a weigh-in!

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.380
Don't eat too much, or it'll
 affect your match tomorrow.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.880
Take it easy, got it?

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.010
Right.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:37.890
Now then,

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.220
how did Aoki do?

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.290
Wow, you should have been there.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.800
It was like both of them were out for blood.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.380
So things <i>did</i>  get rocky. I had a
 feeling it would come to that.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.890
You knew all along, didn't you?

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.030
They're too much alike.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:54.740
They are?

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:59.210
They've both won and lost a fair number of fights.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.290
Even their records are similar.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.040
They're alike in a whole lot of ways.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.830
Now I get it.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.910
Are you sure?

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.500
They're a veritable odd couple. I just don't see it.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.420
What do you think, Senpai?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.170
Ow!

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.980
Hey, focus!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.930
Weren't you even listening?

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.680
Sorry, it's that.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.520
Huh, is that Imae?

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.680
He's with a woman!

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.440
Come on! We can't eavesdrop on them!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.390
Kacchan, you've made weight, haven't you?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.850
I made something to give you nourishment.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.240
I don't want it.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.290
But...

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.960
Why...

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.090
Why did you come to see me?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.450
Now's not the time!

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.980
I'm sorry I broke up with you!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.800
But I'm not naturally gifted!

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.460
When it came down to you or boxing...

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.960
one of you had to go!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.780
Kacchan...

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.680
Every time I remember you,
 I immediately hit the sandbags.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.890
And now I've finally made it to the top!

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.420
I'm sorry...

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.820
I'm sorry.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.450
Sachiko.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.230
Forget you ever knew me.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.000
Boy, what a downer.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.080
I know.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.980
I knew this wasn't a good idea.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.780
They must both still love each other.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.290
But he made a very hard choice.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.750
She even made him food. How heartbreaking.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.750
How could he break up with 
such a raven-haired beauty?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.500
You're right. He's nothing like Aoki.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.230
See?

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.300
I was wrong!

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.680
They're very much alike!

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.680
Aoki's the only maniac who'd 
share <i>that</i> taste in women!

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.270
<i>If... If you can't say something nice...</i>

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.730
I'm home!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.230
Did Masaru come back?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.090
Masaru.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:09.040
That champion, Imae, had the same aura as me.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.160
He even called himself a workhorse.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.580
I know damn well...

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.800
how powerful that word is.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.000
He's learned from all his mistakes, just like me.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.010
He didn't become a champion
 by doing things half-assed!

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.060
I thought I had prepared for the worst.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.620
But now I'm scared!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.510
Come here, Masaru.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.730
I got your courage right here.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.390
Tomiko...

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:51.100
I still can't see anything but a joke of a boxer.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.160
But he <i>did</i>  fight hard for his winning record.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.670
All those moves he created after losing his matches,

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.580
they're the real deal.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.810
He really <i>does</i>  do his homework.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.860
He might even land a Frog Punch.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.680
What's his new move?

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.390
Get a grip on yourself!

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:19.690
You chose boxing over a life with Sachiko!

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.490
You've sacrificed everything, even companionship, in order to become the champion!

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:28.200
And you're afraid of losing it
 all to this damned joker?!

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.330
Not on my watch.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.050
Have you calmed down, Masaru?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.230
Yeah.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.960
God, you're so soft.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.440
<i>I don't shake with fear whenever I'm with you.</i>

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.240
<i>You fill me with courage.</i>

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.970
Tomiko.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:49.210
Will it make you happy if I take the belt?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.180
Of course! I'll be so proud!

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.230
I'll be dating the champion!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.810
Um, but still...

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.980
Champion or not, you're still my Masaru.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.490
You're a wonderful woman, you know that?

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.030
But hold that thought.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.240
I'll make you the proudest woman alive.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.950
I don't need <i>anybody</i>  rooting for me.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:19.090
I will <i>not</i>  give up my belt!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.970
<i>Here's to my first and maybe
 last chance to take the belt.</i>

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.280
<i>And if it  </i>is <i>my last chance, then so be it.</i>

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:38.190
<i>Once the sun sets and day turns to night,</i>

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>they will ring my bell</i>

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.270
<i>of destiny!</i>

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.870
You're looking good.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:55.930
I have to for my rookie title matches.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.620
I can't afford to slip up.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.400
My dad said he's coming to watch.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.380
It won't look good if I lose.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.450
<i>So the master will make his arrival, eh?</i>

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.420
<i>I need to make my proper greetings.</i>

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.440
Well, we <i>do</i>  have a full house tonight.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.830
I'm raring to go.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.430
You've got me to thank for the packed arena!

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.560
Aoki-san!

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:16.890
Man, you're late!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.010
We needed you here to be on standby!

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:21.290
This is the first time I'm headlining.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.490
I need time to steel myself!

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:24.590
Strange.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:25.670
What do you mean?

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:30.150
I thought you'd show up pissing your pants. Why are you so damn calm?

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.160
Are you really Aoki?

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:36.910
G-Get out of here! Of course I am!

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.680
What're you hiding?!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.920
H-Hello, everyone!

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.140
T-Tomiko-san!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.550
You were holding hands the whole time?

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.260
I wanted to calm his nerves.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.050
Last night, you guys didn't...

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.150
bump uglies, did you?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.360
Why the silent treatment?!

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.750
We told you that'd just waste your stamina!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.900
I'm sorry!

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.440
He took another blow!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.440
Is his opponent that good?

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.690
N-No,

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.910
something's clearly wrong with Manabu-kun!

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.300
Go get him!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.000
Ma-Na-Poot!

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:23.290
Ma-Na-Poot!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.240
Ma-Na-Poot!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:24.790
What the?!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:25.250
Eww!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.920
<i>Dammit! My body's not moving right!</i>

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.920
<i>Did I eat and drink too much yesterday?</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.930
Itagaki! Quit standing around and move your feet!

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.470
Mana-

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.690
What the? Is Itagaki struggling?

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.820
It'll be all right, Masaru.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.160
T-Tomiko...

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.720
Tomiko...

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.620
You're so needy, Masaru.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:05.500
Tomiko...

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.300
<i>He's brought a woman to his title match?!</i>

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:13.210
<i>I've never felt so angry before a fight!</i>

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.090
Tomiko, I'm fine now.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.590
It's almost time for my match.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:23.100
I'm gonna hit the head.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.240
So you're confident enough to bring a date?

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.600
You saw us?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.590
That woman's too good for me.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.920
My girlfriend was a good woman as well.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:45.750
"Was"?

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:47.860
I broke it off with her.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.960
I needed to focus on boxing.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:55.130
Unlike you, I do not enter the ring capriciously.

00:11:55.870 --> 00:12:00.260
Tonight, I will show you how my 
adherence to boxing eclipses yours.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.290
Why are you laughing?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.140
Now I get it.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:10.400
So that's why you constantly look like you're about to pop a vessel.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.650
You kicked her to the curb?

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:15.280
Your goddess of victory?

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:22.700
I'll show you how powerful a guy can be when she's looking over him.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.370
Then show me, damn it!

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:31.240
Y-You stupid twat!

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.340
Finish up before facing me!

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:37.630
Only 30 seconds remain in this tumultuous 4th round!

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:40.420
Will Itagaki be completely dominated?

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:50.900
<i>Now!</i>

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.570
There goes Itagaki!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.280
He lands a counter!

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:12.690
He's done it!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:16.130
He gets in a powerful KO at the very last minute!

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:19.010
Itagaki Manabu comes out on
 top in this fierce struggle!

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.650
You did it, Manabu-kun!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.430
Good grief.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.390
You did great, Mana-poot!

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:38.030
Christ Almighty, don't scare us like that!

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.410
Ow! Oww...

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.640
You were way down on points.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.140
But you came from behind with a KO.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.990
I was really worried there.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.540
Aoki-san! I won!

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.520
Wh... What...

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.920
...on earth are you doing?

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:59.170
I, uh, had a little accident, but she's taking care of it.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.250
Asshole!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.090
You <i>trying</i>  to pollute our sacred sport?

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.810
Keep your hanky-panky <i>out</i>  of the locker room!

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:04.810
Yow!

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:07.180
No, we weren't...

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:12.230
I warmed up the crowd for you.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.060
Go and win it for us!

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:14.560
Right on!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.330
<i>I'm fully prepared for this.</i>

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.190
<i></i>And <i>I got my goddess of victory.</i>

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.190
Good luck, Masaru.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.700
<i>My bell of destiny is ready to ring!</i>

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.500
What's with you guys?

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.880
I thought you looked really dashing.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.140
Me too.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.000
I think you might actually win this.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.380
You sorta looked like you'd kick ass.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.380
Was that supposed to encourage me?

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.940
Come out if you're ready!

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.970
The stage awaits you, Aoki!

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.770
Hell yeah!

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.110
Knock ‘em out!

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:58.150
Yeah!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.790
We now bring you the main event!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:16.580
The Champions Carnival, the Japanese lightweight title match!

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:21.920
Of all the Champions Carnivals we've had this year, this one ranks as one of the most unique crowd-pleasers!

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:35.580
Aoki! Aoki! Aoki!{background, multiple}

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:27.170
And speaking of Korakuen's crowd-
pleasers, here's Aoki Masaru,

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.550
sporting the Victory Frog on his back!

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.560
What kind of performance will he give us in his first title match?

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:36.670
Aoki! Frog the hell out of him!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.270
That's what I'm here for!

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:46.360
<i>The spotlights look brighter than usual.</i>

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:48.660
<i>I've finally made it.</i>

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:53.620
<i>I've always wanted to savor this moment even just once.</i>

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.090
<i>Don't worry, Tomiko.</i>

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.630
<i>I got this.</i>

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.300
<i>I will come out of this ring...</i>

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:07.130
<i>as the champion!</i>

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.430
The challenger points his arms toward...

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.330
the champion, Imae Katsutaka!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.580
He's always made it a point to remain levelheaded,

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:20.940
but in this second title defense, will he retain his cool against a maverick?

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:26.190
Whoa there!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.720
He's up in his face!

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.490
But the challenger doesn't flinch!

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.530
Are they already battling it out?!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.330
Aoki!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.640
Imae.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.080
Hey!

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.170
The two fighters separate.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:42.080
Sparks are flying all over the place as we wait for the bell!

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.340
So that's Aoki-kun?

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.840
I hear he's been looking after my son.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.220
Aoki!

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:50.420
Frog him and knock him out!

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:51.680
You better Frog him!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.800
This is where I come in.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:59.410
If you throw a Frog Punch, you'll leapfrog to victory!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.520
You call that a gag?

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:01.740
That sucked, old dude!

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.480
That... was perfect!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.740
What the hell was that?

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:07.280
Was he rooting for you?

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.700
<i>This is why I hate these comedy shows!</i>

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:12.370
Imae!

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.150
Don't get angry!

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.830
Keep your cool like you always do, you hear?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.700
Understood.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.500
<i>Must concentrate on keeping my belt.</i>

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:24.640
<i>Concentrate... maintain composure.</i>

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.000
<i>Maintain composure.</i>

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.260
Imae's really concentrating on the match.

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:33.360
And here I am tingling from all the tension.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.390
I can feel his pressure from here.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:38.620
Once he takes the initiative, there's no going back.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.950
Trip him up before he establishes his rhythm!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:44.610
You're talking to the master of tripping up boxers.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.610
<i>I'll put everything I have on the mat.</i>

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.570
<i>I'll come in flying once the bell rings!</i>

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:54.660
Shoot, I thought Aoki'd be a lot more jumpy than this.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.890
He's turned defiant, in a good way.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.680
He has his war face on.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.290
I know he'll make it happen.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.540
They're putting in their mouthpieces and getting into their stances.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:10.130
The only thing that can cut through this heavy, ominous thunderhead is...

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:14.260
the bell!

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:22.040
The champion, Imae Katsutaka, takes on the textbook upright stance.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:26.900
This consummate professional controls his matches using steady, precise jabs.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:30.660
Facing him is a real maverick, the challenger Aoki Masaru!

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:36.660
His ever-evolving offensive attacks have delighted both the young and the old from start to finish!

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:45.750
The champion hunkers down and shows no signs of attacking while the maverick hovers around.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.470
The challenger dives in!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.130
No wait, he doesn't!

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.640
He maintains his distance!

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.640
What're you doing?! Frog him already!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:03.590
There's no fight if you don't trade fists!

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.520
Yeah! Kick it off with a Frog!

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.070
This is his first title match!

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.890
At least let him build up momentum!

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.310
Calm down.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.030
They <i>are</i>  rooting for him, you know.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.740
Quit acting so damn important!

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:21.490
I thought your fights were supposed to be screwed up! You're starting to bore me!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.910
Th-That was not a cheer!

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.170
It <i>is</i>  coming from someone we know.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.320
Whose side are you on anyway?!

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:32.970
But Takamura-san is right.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:36.930
He needs to start punching even
 if the fight <i>does</i>  get screwy.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.760
There's... no opening.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.450
Opening?

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.220
Aoki's a seasoned veteran, you know.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.180
He may not be hitting yet,

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.310
but he's been juking and weaving trying to establish his own pace.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:55.240
Yet it looks like Imae's even more professional than advertised.
